# tools/cr/crypto_ed25519_group_witness.rish — the edwards25519 group law authored in pure Rye, composed entirely over the GREEN base field
# (crypto/fe25519.rye): Season G's seventh rung, point add and double over the proven field, proven against algebraic known-answers and
# byte-for-byte against an independent implementation (Season G · Cryptography).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season G thread (Cryptography · Rye-native, Monocypher-parity, audit-ready).
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-193010_fe25519-the-curve-field-crux.md (the field this stands on) and
# active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (Season G names Ed25519 as the Lotus unblock, its group
# arithmetic a composition over the field).
# Kin: crypto/fe25519.rye (the base field, GREEN) · crypto/poly1305.rye · crypto/aead.rye. Monocypher (vendor/monocypher, CC0/BSD-dual) is
# the parity TARGET, never a copied line — our own composition, studied clean-room from the public mathematics of twisted Edwards curves
# and Monocypher's public API (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# crypto/ed25519_group.rye carries a point in extended twisted-Edwards coordinates (X, Y, Z, T) so addition and doubling are complete and
# inversion-free; the one inversion lives at compression, where a point becomes the 32-byte Y/Z with the sign of X/Z in the top bit (RFC
# 8032 §5.1). The curve constant 2d is derived in our own field arithmetic (d = −121665/121666), never a copied literal. The primitive
# calls no std.crypto. Parity is proven at selftest against two references runnable now: algebraic known-answers (the base point compresses
# to its published encoding, the identity to Y = 1, B + B = 2B, and B + (−B) = the identity), and Zig's own std.crypto.ecc.Edwards25519 as
# an independent implementation, byte-for-byte on the compression of dbl, add, sub, and neg across the base point and several of its
# multiples. The vendored Monocypher source is a held network fetch, so Monocypher-source parity is an honest horizon rung. Purely local —
# a curve point is arithmetic, not a secret and not a signature: no real key, no signing (Ed25519's signing stays its own gated round, even
# the scalar ladder a later non-gated round), no network, no funds, no real device; constant-time timing-safety a separate named horizon.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cr/crypto_ed25519_group_witness.rish

say "crypto-ed25519-group: Language EN — Season G's seventh rung: the edwards25519 group law authored in pure Rye, composed entirely over the GREEN base field (crypto/fe25519.rye). Ed25519 signing — the Lotus signed carry, Kumara identity, Vault, Comlink — adds a point to itself many times over this curve; that ladder is a composition over exactly two operations, point addition and point doubling, and this rung authors both. It is pure arithmetic — no key, no signature, no identity, no custody gate — so once it is parity-GREEN, scalar multiplication becomes a composition over dbl and add."
say "crypto-ed25519-group: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: a point rides in extended twisted-Edwards coordinates (X, Y, Z, T) with x = X/Z, y = Y/Z, and T = XY/Z, the representation that makes addition and doubling complete and inversion-free; the one inversion lives at compression, where a point becomes the little-endian Y/Z with the low bit of X/Z folded into the top bit (RFC 8032 §5.1). The curve constant 2d, where d = −121665/121666, is derived in our own field arithmetic so no borrowed literal enters the tree."
say "crypto-ed25519-group: Lens TAME — the primitive calls no std.crypto; it composes over fe25519's proven public API, never inverting a field element inside the group law, and asserts its contracts on every function. Parity holds against algebraic known-answers AND Zig's independent std.crypto.ecc.Edwards25519 byte-for-byte on the compression of dbl, add, sub, and neg across the base point and several of its multiples. Monocypher-source parity is a named horizon behind the held vendor fetch. Purely local — a curve point is not a secret and not a signature, so no real key, no signing, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays a separate named horizon."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/ed25519_group"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/ed25519_group.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-ed25519-group: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/ed25519_group.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-ed25519-group: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-ed25519-group: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-ed25519-group' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-ed25519-group: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-ed25519-group line"
